# Stimuli: ~605MB of house images. Needed to run the experiment, too big for
# git. See STIMULI.md.
experiment/stimuli/*
**/stimuli/house_images/

# Participant and practice data. These should normally live outside a clean
# clone, but stay ignored if a rig-local checkout creates them.
experiment/Data/
experiment/Data_practice/
!experiment/Data/README.md

# MATLAB
*.asv
*.mat
*.fig

# Analysis outputs
*.jasp
*.omv
outputs/
figures/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# OneDrive sync-conflict copies
*-ASCPSY-*
*[Cc]onflicted*
* - Copy.*
~$*

# NTFS alternate data streams
*:*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ...but the stimulus lists define the design, so they are tracked
!experiment/stimuli/*.csv
!experiment/stimuli/README.md
!experiment/stimuli/prepare_stimuli.py
!experiment/stimuli/prepared/
!experiment/stimuli/prepared/*.csv
!experiment/stimuli/prepared/*.json
!experiment/stimuli/stimgen/
!experiment/stimuli/stimgen/configs/
!experiment/stimuli/stimgen/configs/*.json

# Researcher-facing material, deliberately absent from the RA's clone
# (2026-10-01). The RAs run sessions from physical run-sheets; grant PDFs, a
# .pptx, meeting notes, three other people's prior studies and the HTML setup
# deck were 66 of 180 tracked files and none of it is needed to run a session.
# Several of them (docs/grant/, reference/*/Data/) should not be in an
# RA-visible clone at all, separate from the clutter.
#
# These files still exist on Murray's disk and in git history up to 99e6cce --
# `git show 99e6cce:docs/grant/...` retrieves any of them. They are untracked,
# not deleted. Re-add with `git add -f <path>` when the study goes to
# publication or open access, which is the plan.
#
# NOT removed: experiment/README.md stays, because scripts/verify_static.sh
# asserts eight patterns inside it and it is the live design documentation.
# Leading slashes matter here: a bare `README.md` would also match
# experiment/README.md, analysis/README.md and experiment/stimuli/README.md,
# all three of which are kept.
/docs/
/reference/
/README.md
/AGENTS.md
/WORK.md
/STIMULI.md

# Raw data and media live here but are not tracked. CDMLab_HouseAuctionEyeTracking.mp4
# alone is 33MB, and GitHub rejects pushes over 100MB per file. Data belongs in
# the project that produced it, but not in its git history.
data/

# Demo and analysis output. demo_battery.m writes a throwaway session tree;
# run_all.R writes figures and combined CSVs. Both are regenerable from the
# scripts that produce them, and the demo tree holds fake participant 9999
# runs that must never be mistaken for data.
experiment/Data_demo/
analysis/Data_simulated/
analysis/output/

# Share-only folders from the retired pre-git layout. Harmless elsewhere.
Archive/
screen_recordings/

# Isolated development checkouts
.worktrees/
